body:
When using foveation in Metal, [encoder.setViewports()](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/metal/mtlrendercommandencoder/setviewports(_:)) has to be set to the logical texture size (the screen size), not the actual texture size.

For example, when rendering to Compositor Services with foveation enabled, the actual texture size provided by the system is 1888 x 1792, but the `rateRasterizationMap` maps that into the logical screen texture of 4338 x 3478 size. The viewports must be set to this latter size.

Here are additional details about how foveated rendering works in Metal:

https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Metal/rendering-at-different-rasterization-rates
https://developer.apple.com/documentation/metal/scaling-variable-rasterization-rate-content

For the purposes of this PR, the size returned by `get_render_target_size()` is not needed in the Metal rendering pipeline, and can be ignored. But we must set the viewports.

Given the current implementation of `draw_list_begin()` uses the render region to calculate the viewports
```
	if (p_region != Rect2() && p_region != Rect2(Vector2(), viewport_size)) { // Check custom region.
		Rect2i viewport(viewport_offset, viewport_size);
		Rect2i regioni = p_region;
		if (!((regioni.position.x >= viewport.position.x) && (regioni.position.y >= viewport.position.y) &&
					((regioni.position.x + regioni.size.x) <= (viewport.position.x + viewport.size.x)) &&
					((regioni.position.y + regioni.size.y) <= (viewport.position.y + viewport.size.y)))) {
			ERR_FAIL_V_MSG(INVALID_ID, "When supplying a custom region, it must be contained within the framebuffer rectangle");
		}

		viewport_offset = regioni.position;
		viewport_size = regioni.size;
	}
```

it seems logical to extend `XRInterface.get_render_region()` to have a view index parameter, and then propagate the viewports from there. But then the check that render_region must be inside the viewport defined by the `framebuffer->size` no longer applies.

Do you still agree this is a good plan?

---

@clayjohn @stuartcarnie:

Currently I am passing the viewports like this:

```
		RD::DrawListID draw_list = RD::get_singleton()->draw_list_begin(framebuffer, load_color ? RD::DRAW_CLEAR_DEPTH : (RD::DRAW_CLEAR_COLOR_0 | RD::DRAW_CLEAR_DEPTH), c, 0.0f, 0, p_render_data->render_region, breadcrumb);
		if (p_render_data->xr_viewports.size() == 2) {
			RD::get_singleton()->draw_list_set_viewports(draw_list, p_render_data->xr_viewports);
			RD::get_singleton()->draw_list_set_empty_scissor(draw_list);
		}
```

to avoid modifying `draw_list_begin()` signature, but another option could be changing the signature to receive a vector of render regions. What do you think the best solution is?

