body:
I have prototyped using `get_render_region_for_view()` in [this branch](https://github.com/rsanchezsaez/godot/tree/apple/visionos-xr-regions), and for some reason the engine doesn't like it. It results in partial rendering where only the top left part of the screen is rendered, with some graphic artifacts around the borders that seem to indicate we're using the GPU incorrectly.

I think part of the reason is that the `region` is not only used to set the viewports, but it's also used in other parts of the pipeline as `viewport_size` is passed at the end of `draw_list_begin()` to `draw_graph.add_draw_list_begin()` and `_draw_list_start()`.

```
RenderingDevice::DrawListID RenderingDevice::draw_list_begin(RID p_framebuffer, BitField<DrawFlags> p_draw_flags, VectorView<Color> p_clear_color_values, float p_clear_depth_value, uint32_t p_clear_stencil_value, const Rect2 &p_region, uint32_t p_breadcrumb) {

// ...

	draw_graph.add_draw_list_begin(framebuffer->framebuffer_cache, Rect2i(viewport_offset, viewport_size), operations, clear_values, stages, p_breadcrumb);
	draw_graph.add_draw_list_usages(resource_trackers, resource_usages);

	// Mark textures as bound.
	draw_list_bound_textures.clear();

	for (int i = 0; i < framebuffer->texture_ids.size(); i++) {
		Texture *texture = texture_owner.get_or_null(framebuffer->texture_ids[i]);
		if (texture == nullptr) {
			continue;
		}

		texture->bound = true;
		draw_list_bound_textures.push_back(framebuffer->texture_ids[i]);
	}

	_draw_list_start(Rect2i(viewport_offset, viewport_size));
#ifdef DEBUG_ENABLED
	draw_list_framebuffer_format = framebuffer->format_id;
#endif
	draw_list_current_subpass = 0;
	draw_list_subpass_count = framebuffer_key.passes.size();

	Rect2i viewport_rect(viewport_offset, viewport_size);
	draw_graph.add_draw_list_set_viewports(viewport_rect);
	draw_graph.add_draw_list_set_scissors(viewport_rect);
```

Conversely, in the currently working version of this PR, the region returned by the visionOS XR is an empty rectangle, so the "viewport" as seen by `draw_list_begin` is `framebuffer->size`, and then I only override the viewports after the fact (as you noted). This approach seems to work fine.

I don't know why exactly setting the viewport to the logical bigger size is breaking rendering in the branch above, and I'm still investigating and trying different approaches. Feedback from the rendering team would be much appreciated!

